-- title:
--   Ends and smooth-point stalks from an affine chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and `fieldBar q M'` is the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\bar{\mathbb Q})$ obtained by base change to $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`, while `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the corresponding base change of the full modular function field of level $M'$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q$ with $q = 2$; a natural number $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (this is `A.LiesOverPrime q`); a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\kappa(A) =$ `ResidueField A`, whose members are, by `hW`, exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa(A) \to \kappa(w)$ is surjective), lie on the affine geometric part, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) \in$ `ssJSet q`; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` in `fieldBar q M'`; and a distinguished element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   **Base-field data.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that the contraction $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); the approximation hypothesis `hκ`, that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$; the hypothesis `halgc` that $\kappa(A)$ is algebraically closed; an algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa(A)$; the hypothesis `hdomC` that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), i.e. $\kappa(A)[x_0,x_1]$ modulo the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q (ResidueField A) - 1`, is a domain; and an index $\zeta_{ix} \in$ `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$. Further, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, and a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring, with $\varpi_b \neq 0$ generating its maximal ideal.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on `fieldBar q M'` obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\bar{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   **Quantified data and hypotheses on $(F_0, W_0)$.** For every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$; $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; and the linear disjointness hypothesis holds: for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ (the $c_i$ read in `fieldBar q M'`) forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   **The affine chart.** For every subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` with an $A_b$-algebra structure subject to the following twelve hypotheses: (B1) the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion, i.e. the image in `fieldBar q M'` of $a \in A_b$ is the image of $a$ under $\bar{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`; (B2) $B$ is contained in the compositum $L$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$; (B3) every element of $L$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; (B4) $B$ is formally smooth over $A_b$; (B5) $B$ is of finite presentation over $A_b$; (B6) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; (B7) every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ and its image lies in $W_0$; (B8) $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; (B9) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\varpi_b$: an element $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; (B10) the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $B$; (B11) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (B12) identification of the special fibre: for every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa(A)$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q (ResidueField A) Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) — the fixed field, inside the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing})$, of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta)$ for $\zeta \in C_s$ — such that: $\#C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`; $\ker \rho$ is the ideal generated by $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ restricted to $A_b$ is the reduction $a \mapsto$ `residue A a` followed by $\kappa(A) \to$ `quotField`; every element of `quotField` is a ratio of values of $\rho$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those $z$ whose image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of `CoordRing`; and, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and for $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` $\in B$, the value $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1} f)$ equals the image of $\rho(f)$ under [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$, computed in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   **The prolongation.** For every field $FSS$ with a $\kappa(A)$-algebra structure and every `RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') FSS` $R$ — that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of `fieldBar q M'` together with a surjective homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $FSS$ with kernel the maximal ideal, contracting to $A$ on $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, compatible with the reduction of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f$ has a scalar multiple in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue — satisfying that for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_0$, the following holds.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa(A)$, an assignment $Q \mapsto S_Q$ of subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, an assignment $Q \mapsto \varphi_Q$ of ring homomorphisms $A_b[T] \to S_Q$, an assignment $Q \mapsto \chi_Q$ of ring homomorphisms $S_Q \to \kappa(A)$, and an assignment $Q \mapsto D_Q$ of sets of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, such that:
--
--   1.
--
--   $\#N = q + 1$.
--
--   2.
--
--   For every place $Q \notin N$: (a) the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_Q$; (b) $\varphi_Q(C a)$ is that image, for every $a \in A_b$; (c) $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(C a))$ is the reduction of $a$ in $\kappa(A)$; (d) $\chi_Q(\varphi_Q(T)) = 0$; (e) $S_Q$ carries a local ring structure for which $\ker \chi_Q$ is the maximal ideal; (f) $S_Q$ is contained in the compositum $L$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$; (g) every element of $L$ is a ratio of two elements of $S_Q$ with nonzero denominator; (h) $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; (i) $S_Q$ is contained in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and an element $f \in S_Q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $\varphi_Q(C\,\varpi_b)$ divides $f$ in $S_Q$; (j) for every $f \in S_Q$, $f$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its residue $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue of $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ at $Q$ equals the image of $\chi_Q(f)$ under $\kappa(A) \to \kappa(Q)$; (k) the image of $\varphi_Q(T)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and $\mathrm{ord}_Q(R.\mathrm{residue}(\varphi_Q(T))) = 1$; (l) a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $D_Q$ precisely when $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every $f \in S_Q$ one has $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ less than $1$ if and only if $\chi_Q(f) = 0$.
--
--   3.
--
--   The sets $D_Q$ separate the places outside $N$: if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some place $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$, then $Q = Q'$.
--
--   4.
--
--   For every $Q \notin N$ and every $P \in D_Q$, the order $\mathrm{ord}_P$ of the image of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` in `fieldBar q M'` is non-negative.
--
--   5.
--
--   Equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof $h_\tau$ that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$: the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ hτ` of $FSS$ over $\kappa(A)$ satisfies, for every place $Q$, that `R.resAut τ hτ • Q` lies in $N$ if and only if $Q$ does, and, when $Q \notin N$, that `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (Db Q)` — the set of places $P$ with $\tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D_Q$ — equals $D_{\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q}$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the extraction from an affine chart of the $q+1$ ends of the supersingular component of the semistable model and of the local stalks, with an étale coordinate $\varphi_Q$ and residue character $\chi_Q$, at its smooth points, together with the residue discs $D_Q$ above them and their compatibility with the level automorphisms. It is used in the construction of the supersingular discrete valuation data at $k$-level in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks_of_eq_two_of_dvd), and is assembled from the companion results on surjectivity and kernel of the prolongation residue, on the ends, on the smooth-point stalks and on the residue discs in the same case.
